    "metatext": {
        "metatext:research_aim": "CLPB is a putative protein disaggregase localized in the mitochondrial intermembrane space.Loss-of-function mutations in CLPB in humans have been associated with the recently described autosomal recessive multisystem disease 3-methylglutaconic aciduria (MEG-CANN syndrome). To study in vivo role of CLPB we have generated brain specific KO of CLPB (ClpB-nes-cre). As CLPB function is necessary for the maintenance of mitochondrial proteostasis, lack of this protein leads to proteomics changes that we would like to investigate in vivo in brain tissue of the ClpB-nes-cre knockout mice.",
        "metatext:experimental_procedure": "Brain tissue was dissected and tissued were grinded using a pestle and mortar . 2  portions using a spatula tip were submitted. "
    },
